cf","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which book of the Bible marks the beginning of the Old Testament?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Genesis also contains the stories of Noah and Abraham, making it the starting point for many foundational biblical narratives.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7dae-8814-22329144d4e4","description":"Genesis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7923-ac4a-e526469a0f86","description":"Exodus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7e11-bda7-03c2a3503a80","description":"Leviticus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7246-9ce5-ef27682d2310","description":"Numbers","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7bab-a235-7f5ecfcd1a78","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which animal would you associate with the Evernote logo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Evernote\u2019s logo uses an elephant with one ear folded over, echoing a turned-down page corner.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7a2f-99a0-d11469397842","description":"Elephant","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7040-8bd8-8dcbabe68208","description":"Penguin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7398-b629-2139da091e5d","description":"Eagle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7243-a5df-64075a6e8e14","description":"Peacock","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7ba2-8684-a59a1683426f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What do people mean when typing the letters \'POV\' in a message on the internet?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Point of View is also used in writing and film to describe whose eyes a story or scene is shown through. Online, it often introduces an imagined scenario.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-76aa-921c-f797719f1ee2","description":"Point of View","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7e2e-9805-7635e1c5ce7f","description":"Plants or Vegetation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7af6-8191-df354e20401a","description":"Perform on Video","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7793-93c1-37a84e689dc6","description":"Play on Vine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7358-aa6c-84a832f26f27","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes Michelangelo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Michelangelo was a Renaissance sculptor, painter and architect who also designed the dome of St. Peter\u2019s Basilica; it was completed after his death.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-73a6-8e59-2f0d4ff5cbff","description":"Renaissance sculptor, painter and architect","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7950-91a6-53ee8fe4b2b9","description":"Founder of Manichaeism, a gnostic religion which for a time was a rival to Christianity.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7d11-91a7-18cf02d069f7","description":"Inventor and businessman who helped introduce electricity and electric light bulbs.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7fc6-85fd-98c955044a56","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7495-a260-baa828eb4c7d","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the marketing slogan of Audi?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Audi\'s German tagline is \u201cVorsprung durch Technik,\u201d commonly rendered in English as \u201cAdvancement Through Technology.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7051-937c-6fde5e4583dd","description":"Advancement Through Technology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7615-aba0-9dd6ee7a98ae","description":"Grace, Space, Pace.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-70ba-88bb-485882c9e505","description":"There is no substitute","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7238-821d-41b3a858a2ea","description":"Think Small","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7d01-8c17-8e2296e142eb","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes Asoka?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Asoka was a Mauryan ruler whose rock and pillar edicts promoted moral conduct and tolerance after the Kalinga war.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7ecc-bc8d-ecda943a1142","description":"Powerful Indian King who established a large empire by conquest before converting to Buddhism.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-749c-8511-7dd68adb0e04","description":"Queen of England from 1558 to her death in 1603. Cemented England as a Protestant country, defeated Spanish Armada.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7aad-8676-6b170f34c6fc","description":"Explorer, first European to reach India and establish a route for imperialism.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7435-8fb4-e8999332cd8f","description":"Spiritual Teacher and founder of Buddhism.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7974-aad1-13a1cce7a2d8","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What did \'my true love give to me\' on the ninth day of Christmas?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The ninth gift is 9 Ladies Dancing, placed after eight maids a-milking and before ten lords a-leaping in the cumulative song.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7810-be3a-3fc3cc571c47","description":"9 Ladies Dancing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7e6c-b021-e2a06bdcba2e","description":"9 Lords a Leaping","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7a58-ad7e-dfaf0afe614d","description":"9 Calling Birds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7de6-b9a7-6c02dabdf596","description":"9 Pipers Piping","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae92-7132-8b91-8aab89940841","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What title does the head of government hold in countries with a Westminster system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A prime minister usually leads the Cabinet and is accountable to the legislature; a monarch, where one exists, is typically head of state.","a